.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt HEXDUMP 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm hexdump
.Nd display a stream of bytes in conventional formats
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bcCdox
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl n Ar length
.Op Fl s Ar skip
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This bounded adaptation of Toybox 0.8.15 concatenates the named files;
no file or a dash reads standard input. Default and -x display little-endian
two-byte hexadecimal; -b byte octal; -c escaped characters; -d two-byte decimal;
-o two-byte octal; -C hexadecimal and ASCII. Modes are mutually exclusive.
-v expands repeats; -n limits displayed bytes, including zero; -s skips across
file boundaries. Partial final blocks are displayed.
Numbers are unsigned decimal or hexadecimal with optional Toybox size suffixes.
.Xr toybox 7
records origin and license.
.Sh LIMITS
Custom -e and -f formats are refused. Counters use checked unsigned 64-bit
arithmetic. Streaming buffers are fixed; processing time scales with input.
Reported I/O errors return 2; success returns 0. External termination is
separate, including Linux SIGPIPE on a closed output pipe.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr od 1 ,
.Xr diff 1 ,
.Xr toybox 7
